  "contract": [
    "Explicit hostclock.Observe reads native synchronization and uncertainty evidence outside request handling. It changes no clock settings.",
    "Linux uses adjtimex with zero modes and a CLOCK_BOOTTIME elapsed counter. macOS uses ntp_gettime and CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW backed by mach_continuous_time.",
    "Both adapters reject unsafe synchronization or leap states, malformed timestamps, and excessive uncertainty. Arithmetic rejects overflow before conversion.",
    "Elapsed reads do not open files or send network requests. Both native elapsed allocation checks report zero allocations.",
    "Windows remains unsupported and supplies no usable observation or elapsed counter.",
    "No adapter selects a qualified production drift/error profile or starts a scheduler. Host composition remains required."
  ],
